PART 1 -- THE TRANSLATION TABLE: each claim -> its distribution form
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

(a) M_dark = M_b r/r_M  ->  the dark-mass distribution's EXPECTATION
    phantom rho ~ r^-2  =>  dM/dr = const: the mass elements' radii are
    UNIFORM on (0, r_M):  f_R(r) = 1/r_M,  F_R(r) = P(R < r) = r/r_M,
    E[M_dark(<r)] = M_b P(R < r) = M_b r/r_M.  The enclosed dark mass is
    M_b TIMES THE CDF OF THE RADIUS DISTRIBUTION.
  [PASS] equipartition = uniform-radius CDF: dM/dr const, E[M_dark(<r)] = M_b (r-r_in)/(r_M-r_in) exactly
         measured: max|M(<r)/M_b - (r-r_in)/(r_M-r_in)| = 2.22e-16 over [0.3 kpc, r_M]
         reading : G154/G227: the Gauss-map M_ph(<r) = (1/4piG) oint g.dA = M_b r/r_M certified in Lean 5.
    r_M(MW, 7e10 Msun) = 10.21 kpc; the phantom's own field g = C/r with C = sqrt(G M_b a0), so u = g_obs/2a0 = r_M/(2r) along the profile.

