    the distribution's landmarks (u = g_obs/2a0 -> r = r_M/(2u)):
      mode of dP/dlog10u: u = 0.4989  ->  r = r_M  (THE BOUNDARY)
      median of U        : u = 0.4142  ->  r = 1.207 r_M
      quartiles          : u = 0.1547/0.4142/1.0000  ->  r = 3.23/1.21/0.50 r_M
      survival at r_M    : P(U > 1/2) = (1+1/2)^-2 = 0.4444; inside r_M (u > 1/2) the
      CDF sits near saturation (Newtonian side, mu -> 1); outside r_M the distribution
      enters its power-law tail (deep-MOND side, mu ~ 2u).

----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
PART 2 -- THE KERNEL'S ROLE: the RAR is a quantile-quantile statement
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    g_N = g_obs mu_2(g_obs/2a0), mu_2 = CDF of the mass-weighted OBSERVED-
    acceleration distribution (H055: 1-mu_2 = (1+u)^-2, u = g_obs/2a0):
    g_N/g_obs = P(U <= g_obs/2a0) -- the ratio IS the quantile; every
    (g_obs, g_N) point lies ON the CDF curve (a QQ relation).
    THE DEEP LINE g_obs^2 = a0 g_N  <=>  g_N/g_obs = g_obs/a0 = F(g_obs/2a0)
    in the linear tail F(x) ~ 2x for x << 1: the deep line is the CDF's
    LINEAR REGIME, exact in the tail of the committed kernel.
  [PASS] deep line = tail of the CDF: g_N = g_obs mu(g_obs/a0) with mu ~ g_obs/a0 for g_obs << a0 gives g_obs^2 = a0 g_N asymptotically
         measured: max |g_obs^2/(a0 g_N) - 1| over y = g_obs/a0 in [1e-6, 1e-2] = 7.506e-03 (leading correction -3y/4: 7.5e-03 at y = 1e-2)
    IS THE DEEP LINE THE MEDIAN OR THE MODE?  It is the CONDITIONAL MEAN of
    log10 g_obs at fixed g_N (the law's expectation; zero-mean residual by
    construction).  It coincides with the conditional median -- and with the
    mode, for unimodal residuals -- IFF the residual distribution is symmetric.
    DECIDED BY THE MEASURED RESIDUALS:
      542-object line residuals: skewness -0.581, mean-median gap -0.0045 dex
      -> the residuals are effectively symmetric about the line (skew -0.58 but mean = median to 0.004 dex): the deep line is simultaneously the conditional mean, median and mode

